Audit this code for security issues (Node/JS):

app.get('/img', (req, res) => {
  res.sendFile('/var/www/' + req.query.name);
});

output:
**Vulnerability:** Path traversal
**Severity:** High
**Why:** The name is appended to a base path without confinement.
**Exploit:** `?name=../../etc/passwd`.
**Fix:**
const path = require('path');
const base = '/var/www';
const target = path.resolve(base, req.query.name);
if (!target.startsWith(base + path.sep)) return res.sendStatus(403);
res.sendFile(target);

